From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 00:09:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/57] panvk: Handle clip distances as general varyings

The varying setup matches VS outputs and FS inputs by location, and
with VK_EXT_shader_object both stages can be compiled without seeing
each other. Clip distances therefore have to stay at their own
locations, CLIP_DIST0/1. Remapping them to VAR slots per stage could
pick a different slot in each stage.

The varying layout code already assigns a byte offset to any slot that
is not a hardware varying. Only two panvk sites treated everything
below VARYING_SLOT_VAR0 as a hardware varying, which left clip
distances at byte offset zero where they collided with VAR0. Check
against PAN_HARDWARE_VARYING_BITS instead.

Pass the VS clip distance array size to the backend, and run the FS
clip distance lowering on fragment shaders.

Signed-off-by: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Reviewed-by: Olivia Lee <olivia.lee@collabora.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/40343>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
index 77b61ac438c..6045ba6184e 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 #include "compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.h"
 #include "compiler/pan_compiler.h"
 #include "compiler/pan_nir.h"
+#include "compiler/pan_nir_prolog.h"
 #include "pan_shader.h"
 
 #include "vk_log.h"
@@ -1621,6 +1622,8 @@ panvk_compile_shader(struct panvk_device *dev,
             inputs.varying_layout = &varying_layout;
          }
 
+         inputs.clip_distance_array_size = nir->info.clip_distance_array_size;
+
          if (v == PANVK_VS_VARIANT_SW)
             panvk_nir_lower_compute_vs(nir, inputs.gpu_id);
 
@@ -1735,6 +1738,8 @@ panvk_compile_shader(struct panvk_device *dev,
       nir_assign_io_var_locations(nir, nir_var_shader_out);
       panvk_lower_nir_io(nir);
 
+      NIR_PASS(_, nir, pan_nir_lower_clip_distance_fs);
+
       /* Lower FS outputs now so that we can lower load_blend_descriptor_pan
        * to a driver-provided FAU instead of using the blend descriptors
        * uploaded by the hardware.  See panvk_vX_blend.c for details.
@@ -2558,7 +2563,7 @@ emit_varying_attrs(struct panvk_pool *desc_pool,
             gl_varying_slot loc = slot->location;
 
             enum pipe_format pfmt = PIPE_FORMAT_NONE;
-            bool is_hw = loc < VARYING_SLOT_VAR0;
+            bool is_hw = (BITFIELD64_BIT(loc) & PAN_HARDWARE_VARYING_BITS) != 0;
             bool is_present = is_hw || bit_sizes[loc] != 0;
 
             if (is_present && !is_hw) {
@@ -2635,7 +2640,7 @@ panvk_per_arch(link_shaders)(struct panvk_pool *desc_pool,
 
       const gl_varying_slot pos = fs_var->location;
       /* Skip special varyings. */
-      if (pos < VARYING_SLOT_VAR0)
+      if (BITFIELD64_BIT(pos) & PAN_HARDWARE_VARYING_BITS)
          continue;
 
       /* Special buffers are handled explicitly before this loop, everything
